From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scott Smith <scott@newtrostudios.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 18:30:22 -0400
Subject: remotesmith(0101): rename to RemoteSmith (bundle, installer, service
 names, about)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Cargo bundle metadata, macOS PRODUCT_NAME/bundle id ai.johnnycode.remotesmith
  (xcconfig, pbxproj, scheme, MainMenu.xib Swift module, Info.plist URL scheme
  remotesmith://), Windows Runner.rc/main.cpp and BINARY_NAME remotesmith.
- build.py copies the service binary into RemoteSmith.app and packs
  remotesmith.exe; MSI preprocess defaults to RemoteSmith, ARP links and the
  license page point at github.com/newtro/RemoteSmith with an AGPL notice that
  credits RustDesk.
- macOS: the embedded launchd plists/scripts and the root-update paths use ORG
  (ai.johnnycode) instead of hard-coded com.carriez, so labels, plist paths and
  the preferences dir all match Config::path() and get_full_name().
- Desktop tab bar title uses the app name; About shows the AGPL notice, the
  RustDesk credit and the source link; "Powered by RustDesk" links to the source.

Plan: DEC-15, §4 thin-fork patch 1, AC-33.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
